> Simple example: pixel-centre crops

A patch classifier needs a fixed input size, while proposed regions have varying
pixel boxes. For side S, output pixel `(r,c)` samples
`y=ymin+(r+.5)*(ymax-ymin)/S-.5` and similarly for x. Bilinear interpolation
uses zero outside the image. A full five-pixel box resized to three pixels
therefore samples source coordinates `1/3,2,11/3`, rather than the endpoints.
For the linear ramp below its first, middle and last values are `1/12,1/2,11/12`.
Cropping keeps tensor gradients; it does not train the classifier.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/detection_baselines_crop.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  const auto image = n::arange(0, 25).to(n::DType::Float64).reshape({1, 5, 5, 1}) / 24.;
  const auto patch = n::models::CropDetectionPatches(
      image, n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{0}),
      n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{0, 0, 5, 5}, {1, 4}), 3);
  if (std::abs(patch.at({0, 0, 0, 0}) - 1. / 12) > 1e-12 ||
      std::abs(patch.at({0, 1, 1, 0}) - .5) > 1e-12 ||
      std::abs(patch.at({0, 2, 2, 0}) - 11. / 12) > 1e-12)
    return 1;
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(image.reshape({5, 5}), 0, 1);
  a.title("Five by five source ramp").x_label("source column").y_label("row from bottom");
  auto b = n::plot_tensor_map(patch.reshape({3, 3}), 0, 1);
  b.title("Three by three centre crop").x_label("output column").y_label("row from bottom");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(a).add(b).size(1200, 550).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/detection_baselines_crop.svg");
  std::print("Pixel-centre crop values: first {:.12f}, middle {:.12f}, last {:.12f}.\n",
             patch.at({0, 0, 0, 0}), patch.at({0, 1, 1, 0}), patch.at({0, 2, 2, 0}));
}
```
