> Data: real MNIST digits on detection canvases

The source scatters one to four MNIST digits, resized to 16–32-pixel cells, onto
64-pixel canvases. Tight boxes surround pixels brighter than byte value 32.
Accepted patches combine by maximum; candidates overlapping an earlier box by
IoU greater than .3 are retried, up to thirty attempts per object. All resize,
quantization, box extrema, overlap checks and compositing use tensors. Integer
sampling metadata retains the source `mt19937_64` draw order. Tensor Float64
interpolation can differ from host arithmetic by one byte at a rounding boundary.

This bounded run uses 80 scenes from the first 2048 official training digits:
64 fit scenes and 16 validation scenes, seed 11. Eight held-out scenes use the
first 512 official test digits and seed 22. The original full example uses
6000/1000 scenes and the complete digit pools; these are teaching-run results.
Green outlines below show actual training annotations. Digits may touch, which
is a difficulty for connected-component proposals.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/detection_baselines_scenes.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("mnist", (cache / "mnist").string());

  const auto train = n::load_mnist((cache / "mnist").string(), "train");
  n::models::DetectionSceneConfig cfg;
  cfg.scenes = 80;
  cfg.seed = 11;
  const auto scenes = n::models::MakeTensorDetectionScenes(
      n::slice_axis(train.images, 0, 0, 2048), n::slice_axis(train.labels, 0, 0, 2048), cfg);

  std::vector<n::Tensor> boxes(scenes.boxes.begin(), scenes.boxes.begin() + 8);
  const auto preview = n::models::DrawDetectionBoxes(n::slice_axis(scenes.images, 0, 0, 8),
                                                     boxes, {.1, 1., .2});
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(preview, "build/detection_baselines_scenes.png", 4, 0., 1., 4, 1., 2);
  std::int64_t objects = 0;
  for (const auto &b : scenes.boxes)
    objects += b.shape()[0];
  std::print("80 generated training/validation scenes; {} accepted digits. Preview: first "
             "eight training scenes with tight green boxes.\n",
             objects);
}
