Patch sampling makes three jittered square crops per object, plus up to three
random backgrounds per object whose maximum target IoU is at most .2. Jitter
changes side by a factor in `[1,1.3)` and centre by at most .1 of the sampled
side. Background sides range from 12 to 40 pixels. Tensor RNG supplies these
continuous draws, so its sequence differs explicitly from the legacy host RNG.
There is no fitting inside the sampler. Class 10 is background.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/detection_baselines_patches.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
